# One-time world works (life/works.js): the Dwarven Road (life/trade_roads.js) and the planted forests round Tempest and
# Treyni's shrine (life/forests.js). They run once, about 2 minutes after a start and after the landmarks and builds, so on
# the first boot after the deploy the @until lines wait for them (the road takes about a minute, the forests a few); on
# every later run they hold at once. `expect road ... surface <arc>` reads the block at the road's centre at that arc
# length (a chunk load for one chunk): arc 200 is in Lerfing's wood north of Tempest, 1000 at the arrival, 1300 on the
# stone stretch of the Canaat apron.
ttl works list
@until 900 ttl works expect road tempest_dwargon laid
ttl works expect road tempest_dwargon surface 200
ttl works expect road tempest_dwargon surface 1000
ttl works expect road tempest_dwargon surface 1300
@until 1200 ttl works expect forest tempest planted 35
@until 1200 ttl works expect forest treyni planted 45
